# {{pluginName}}

Twilight Echo API v3 declarative theme scaffold.

Use `structured` token IDs, host-registered modes, and the host-owned shell layout for stable visual
overrides.
Unknown modes are ignored with a compatibility note. `variables` and `theme.css`
remain available for API v1 compatibility and advanced styling.

The contract catalog, compatibility matrix, and migration guide are documented in
`docs/theme-plugin-authoring.md` in the Twilight Echo repository.

`create-twilight-plugin` is currently available from the Twilight Echo source tree, not the npm registry. Set up the local development dependency as described in the [plugin development guide](https://github.com/Px-asen/Twilight_Echo/blob/Pxasen/docs/PLUGIN_README.md) before running these commands.

```bash
pnpm test
pnpm run pack
```
